  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 140 PM CDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nThe upper high continues to dominate the forecast through next week. \nThe upper high will remain centered over the Four Corners region \nthrough mid next week before moving southeastward by late week. \nWhile this will continue to suppress most chances for rainfall, \nthere will still be low chances for afternoon isolated storms, \nespecially as a series of weak cold fronts move across the Central \nPlains into the Southern Plains. Most if not all fronts are progged \nto at best only make it as far south as the Texas Panhandle, but a \nfew storms could still form from remnant outflow boundaries. Overall \nchances are too low for a mention in the forecast. Temperatures will \nbe fairly steady in the mid/upper 90s on the Caprock and low 100s \noff the Caprock through much of the forecast period. Warmer \ntemperatures are expected by late next week as the upper high moves \noverhead.",
